Output: True

nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]
Output: False

nums = [1, 1, 1, 3, 3, 4]
Output: True
  
Write the Python function.

Try solving it without nested loops.

Explain why your approach is efficient.

Tell me its time and space complexity.
"""

#solution- myself - hash set

def solution(arr):
  seen= set()
  for x in arr:
    if x in seen:
      return True
    seen.add(x)
  return False

"""
Time	O(n)
Space	O(n)
